    {
      "index": 3,
      "id": "motivation",
      "heading": "Motivation",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "chunk_id": "s03_c01",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s03_c1_authors_take_third_view_neural",
          "text": "The authors take a third view of a neural network. Beyond its weights and its function values, a model can be represented, up to a translation, by its first-order input gradients, that is, the derivatives of the output with respect to the input.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "authors",
            "take",
            "third",
            "view",
            "neural",
            "network",
            "beyond",
            "its",
            "weights",
            "its"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "chunk_id": "s03_c02",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s03_c2_representation_two_attractive_proper",
          "text": "This representation has two attractive properties. First, input gradients are the same size as the input, which is far smaller than the enormous weight vector, so they are much cheaper to compare with a kernel.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "representation",
            "two",
            "attractive",
            "properties",
            "first",
            "input",
            "gradients",
            "same",
            "size",
            "input"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "chunk_id": "s03_c03",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s03_c3_second_forcing_members_different_inp",
          "text": "Second, forcing members to have different input gradients means forcing them to depend on different input features.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "second",
            "forcing",
            "members",
            "different",
            "input",
            "gradients",
            "means",
            "forcing",
            "them",
            "depend"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "chunk_id": "s03_c04",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s03_c4_intuitively_should_make_ensemble_mor",
          "text": "Intuitively, this should make the ensemble more robust, because if members react to complementary patterns, corrupting one pattern will not fool all of them at once.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "intuitively",
            "should",
            "make",
            "ensemble",
            "more",
            "robust",
            "because",
            "members",
            "react",
            "complementary"
          ],
          "required": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "id": "contribution",
      "heading": "Contribution",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "chunk_id": "s04_c01",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s04_c1_makes_three_main_contributions",
          "text": "The paper makes three main contributions.",
